{
  "title": "Reject inventory balance and movement arithmetic outside persisted numeric bounds",
  "description": "Close central inventory arithmetic failure before persistence. InventoryService.IncreaseAsync directly multiplies quantity*cost and adds quantities/TotalCost to tracked stock; DecreaseAsync and ReverseAsync also compute movement and resulting balances without explicit persisted representability guards. Even individually valid source rows can overflow a cumulative balance or DECIMAL mapping, or throw raw decimal overflow after partial tracking. Compute proposed balance/movement values first, validate actual existing EF precision from ErpDbContext.Config.cs read-only (do not guess scales), convert overflow to controlled business error, then apply through existing service. Preserve weighted-average rounding, explicit/source/fallback cost, depletion clamp, reversal signs and existing transaction ownership. No schema change, permission change, new service/ledger or arbitrary SQL. Ensure failed service operations leave tracked stock/movements unchanged and caller transaction rolls back the whole document, including prior rows. Retain existing live identity/menu/customer-scope authority, transactions, source locks, controlled errors and audit. Reject before numbering or persistence, with zero header/detail/source/status mutations. No new permissions, schema, production access, external service or arbitrary SQL. Genuine SQL only on (localdb)\\NEWERP_AutoAcceptance with Integrated Security and a fresh GUID-owned NEWERP_AUTOTEST database; reject wrong/existing targets and never drop/reset. Require safe Release with analyzers/warnings-as-errors, full units and relevant genuine SQL/browser tests; accurately record blockers and do not claim whole-stage acceptance.",
